## ⭐ Interview Follow-up

Q: Why do we check num - 1 instead of num + 1?

Answer:

We only want to start counting from the beginning of each sequence. If num - 1 exists, then the current number is in the middle of a sequence, so we skip it. This ensures every sequence is counted exactly once.
